{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>ha-rot</b> — like <i>harim</i> [mountains], like <i>shnot shanim</i> [years of years]. Perhaps the word <b>ha-rot</b> changes on account of the guttural letter. And others said: the word <b>ha-rot</b> is according to its meaning — they would not give birth to children, so they did not fear to expand their borders." "<b>ba-teru'ah</b> — because Rabbah was taken by force." "<b>ba-se'ar</b> — in a storm wind, because he mentioned 'I will kindle fire.'"], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:44.576420909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}